      "text": "Jams: never.\nWarranty: ten years.\nUtility: complete.\nThe salesperson did not write this. Probably."
    }
  }
}

:: start
image:: office.svg A quiet Monday morning in the break room.
The break room, 8:40 AM. A colleague walks over holding a stapler in each hand and a hopeful expression.
[[Say hello|hello]]

:: hello
speaker:: sales
[open:sales]Inspect the salesperson[/open]. Good morning! Glad I caught you. Five minutes of your time?
speaker:: player
That depends entirely on what you're selling.
speaker:: sales
The Jansen 3000. The last stapler you will ever need.
set:: claims + 1
[[Ask about the price|price]]
[[Sound intrigued|intrigued]]

:: intrigued
speaker:: player
A stapler that claims to be the last one? That is a bold product promise.
speaker:: sales
Bold is our brand, yes. Also we did the research.
set:: claims + 1
[[Okay, tell me about the price|price]]

:: price
speaker:: sales
It is twenty-nine ninety-nine. Which, yes, sounds like a lot for a stapler.
speaker:: player
For a stapler, that is a lot for a stapler.
speaker:: sales
But consider everything you get: one-handed operation, a jam-free mechanism, and it holds two hundred sheets at once.
set:: claims + 1
[[That is a lot of sheets|compare]]
[[Still not convinced|not_convinced]]

:: compare
set:: impressed + 25
speaker:: player
Two hundred sheets. My current stapler gives up after a week of menus.
speaker:: sales
Exactly. Think of the paperclips you will retire early.
speaker:: player
That is... not how paperclips work.
speaker:: sales
The point stands: fewer jams, fewer unhappy desk drawers.
set:: claims + 1
[[Ask about the warranty|warranty]]

:: warranty
set:: impressed + 15
speaker:: sales
Ten-year warranty. If it ever jams, we replace it, no questions asked.
[open:modal.jansen]Read the spec sheet[/open].
speaker:: player
That does remove the main argument against it.
speaker:: sales
And today only, I will throw in a box of mixed staples. The good ones.
[[Check my budget|budget]]
[[Honestly, you have sold me|buy_now]] if:: impressed >= 60

:: budget
set:: decision = interested
set:: impressed + 10
image:: office.svg The afternoon sun arrives and brightens the room.
speaker:: player
Two hundred sheets, a ten-year warranty, and good staples. That is a surprisingly complete offering.
[[Do it. Buy the stapler.|buy_now]]
[[Maybe next quarter|pass]]

:: buy_now
set:: decision = bought
set:: impressed + 20
speaker:: player
Fine. One Jansen 3000. You have earned this sale.
speaker:: sales
You will not regret a single staple.
goto:: endings

:: not_convinced
speaker:: player
A stapler cannot change my life, Alex.
speaker:: sales
I understand completely. But one day a pile of paper will be there, and you will remember me.
goto:: endings

:: pass
speaker:: player
I will think about it. Professionally. After lunch.
speaker:: sales
That is all I ask. The box of staples stays open if you change your mind.
goto:: endings

:: endings [ending]
image:: office.svg The break room settles back into its usual quiet rhythm.
speaker:: player
However it went, the office supply situation was thoroughly discussed today.
-- The end --